{#- Shared shell for every /staff/ page.

    The console started as one long page. Splitting it means the nav has to
    live in ONE place — hence a real Eleventy layout rather than six copies of
    the same header, and rather than injecting it with JavaScript at runtime
    (which is the "page titles pop in late" mistake this project is already
    trying to remove from chaseroush.com).

    Pages set `staffPage` in their front matter; the nav uses it to mark the
    current link. Nothing else needs coordinating.

    AUTH: Cloudflare Access gates /staff* at the edge, so by the time any of
    this renders the visitor is authenticated. There is no sign-in state to
    manage here. -#}
{#- ONE ENTRY FOR THREE SECTIONS. Milestones, giving goals and prayer are the
   same job — the things a ministry publishes about itself — and each is small.
   Three nav entries for three short pages crowded the bar and made them look
   unrelated; one page with tabs keeps them together.

   The comment lives OUT here rather than inside the array: nunjucks parses a
   `set` as one expression, and a comment inside it is a syntax error rather
   than a comment. -#}
{%- set pages = [
  { slug: "index",       url: "/staff/",             label: "Dashboard" },
  { slug: "ministry",    url: "/staff/ministry/",    label: "Ministry" },
  { slug: "stewardship", url: "/staff/stewardship/", label: "Stewardship" },
  { slug: "directory",   url: "/staff/directory/",   label: "Directory" },
  { slug: "resources",   url: "/staff/resources/",   label: "Resources" },
  { slug: "activity",    url: "/staff/activity/",    label: "Activity" },
  { slug: "settings",    url: "/staff/settings/",    label: "Settings" }
] -%}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>{{ staffTitle }} · Thauma Staff</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tokens.css?v={{ "/css/tokens.css" | v }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/staff.css?v={{ "/css/staff.css" | v }}">
<link rel="icon" href="/img/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
</head>
<body class="is-staff" data-staff-page="{{ staffPage }}">

<header class="top"><div class="top-in">
  <a class="mark" href="/staff/">THAUMA<em data-i18n="mark.staff">STAFF</em></a>
  <nav>
    {%- for p in pages %}
    <a href="{{ p.url }}"{% if p.slug == staffPage %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}
       data-i18n="nav.{{ p.slug if p.slug != 'index' else 'dashboard' }}">{{ p.label }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </nav>
  <div class="top-r">
    {#- WHO IS SIGNED IN. Hidden until known, rather than sitting there reading
       "—" as though a value failed to arrive. -#}
    {#- Revealed by staff.js only when the account holds the admin role. A
       console that shows everyone a link to a place most of them are refused
       teaches people to ignore refusals. -#}
    {#- Reads as a DESTINATION, not a role. It said "Administration" while the
       role beside it also said "Administration", so the header showed the same
       word twice and neither looked like a link. -#}
    <a class="area-switch" id="toAdmin" href="/admin/" hidden>
      <span data-i18n="adm.toAdmin">Admin area</span>
      <span class="area-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
    {#- THE WAY OUT OF THE CONSOLE ENTIRELY. Both areas could reach each other
       and neither could reach the site they exist to edit, so the only way to
       look at your own work was to type the address. Opens in its own tab: you
       come here to CHECK the site, not to leave the console, and a plain link
       would throw away an unsaved form to do it. -#}
    <a class="area-switch" href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <span data-i18n="nav.viewSite">Public site</span>
      <span class="area-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
    </a>
    <span class="pill" id="partnerPill" hidden></span>
    <a class="ghost-btn" href="/cdn-cgi/access/logout" data-i18n="nav.signout">Sign out</a>
  </div>
</div></header>

<main>
  <div class="page-head">
    {#- The live/prototype badge is gone: it separated sections reading a
       generated file from those reading the database, and since 2026-08-15
       every page reads the database. A badge on all seven distinguishes
       nothing and trains people to stop reading badges. The .badge styles
       stay — the milestone list uses them for draft and featured. -#}
    <div class="cue">{{ staffNum }} &mdash; <span data-i18n="page.{{ staffPage }}.title">{{ staffTitle }}</span></div>
    <div class="sec-h">
      <h2 data-i18n-html="page.{{ staffPage }}.heading">{{ staffHeading | safe }}</h2>
      {%- if staffHint %}<span class="hint" data-i18n="page.{{ staffPage }}.hint">{{ staffHint }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="rolegate" id="roleNote" hidden>
    Signed in, but the staff data endpoint refused the request. That usually means this
    deploy is missing its <b>ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN</b> / <b>ACCESS_AUD</b> settings.
  </p>

  {{ content | safe }}
</main>

{#- Before everything else: it reads the cached language and rewrites the
   page synchronously, so the console does not render in English and then
   visibly correct itself. -#}
<script src="/js/staff-i18n.js?v={{ "/js/staff-i18n.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/staff.js?v={{ "/js/staff.js" | v }}"></script>
{#- Only the Milestones page needs this; the script no-ops elsewhere. Kept
   separate from staff.js rather than folded in, because the editor is a
   different job from the read-only console and will keep growing. -#}
{% if staffPage == "ministry" %}<script src="/js/staff-rowpanel.js?v={{ "/js/staff-rowpanel.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/staff-milestones.js?v={{ "/js/staff-milestones.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/staff-goals.js?v={{ "/js/staff-goals.js" | v }}"></script>
<script src="/js/staff-prayer.js?v={{ "/js/staff-prayer.js" | v }}"></script>{% endif %}
{% if staffPage == "settings" %}<script src="/js/staff-settings.js?v={{ "/js/staff-settings.js" | v }}"></script>{% endif %}
{#- The embed panel loads on the two pages that AUTHOR what it publishes —
   the roadmap under the milestone editor, the giving progress under the
   goals — rather than on a settings tab away from both. -#}
{% if staffPage == "ministry" %}<script src="/js/staff-embed.js?v={{ "/js/staff-embed.js" | v }}"></script>{% endif %}
</body>
</html>
